From: DroidDeck FEX audit <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] HostFeatures: only take the SVE128 paths when SVE vectors are 128 bits wide

OverrideFeatures() turns SupportsSVE256 off unless ForceSVEWidth asks for it,
while SupportsSVE128 stays on for any SVE2 host. The SVE128 paths operate on
whole Z registers (uunpkhi/sunpkhi, gathers, wide shifts) and are only right
when those are 128 bits wide: on a host with longer vectors they take in the
upper lanes too.

Reproduced under qemu-aarch64 8.2.2 with -cpu max,sme=off and
sve-default-vector-length=32 or 64, FEX-2610 (14c92681f):
  pmaddubsw xmm0, xmm1        upper four words come out 0
  vcvtdq2pd ymm2, xmm2        upper two doubles come from the wrong lane
  unittests/ASM/VEX/vcvtdq2pd.asm fails; passes at sve-default-vector-length=16
With this change those match an x86-64 host at 128, 256 and 512 bits.

Hosts with SVE2 at 128 bits (Cortex-X2..X925, Neoverse N2/V2) are unchanged.
The Windows frontends never enable SVE and are unaffected.

---
diff --git a/Source/Common/HostFeatures.cpp b/Source/Common/HostFeatures.cpp
index 858d76d71..0dd576683 100644
--- a/Source/Common/HostFeatures.cpp
+++ b/Source/Common/HostFeatures.cpp
@@ -597,6 +597,14 @@ void FetchHostFeatures(FEX::CPUFeatures& Features, FEXCore::HostFeatures& HostFe
 
   HandleErrata(&HostFeatures, MIDR);
   OverrideFeatures(&HostFeatures, ForceSVEWidth());
+
+#ifndef VIXL_SIMULATOR
+  // The SVE128 paths work on whole Z registers, which is only right when they are 128 bits wide. On a
+  // wider host without the SVE256 paths enabled they would also take in the upper lanes; use ASIMD there.
+  if (HostFeatures.SupportsSVE128 && !HostFeatures.SupportsSVE256 && Features.GetSVEVectorLengthInBits() != 128) {
+    HostFeatures.SupportsSVE128 = false;
+  }
+#endif
 }
 
 FEXCore::HostFeatures FetchHostFeatures() {
